    "sentence_translations": [
      "When you have nothing, you have nothing to lose",
      "",
      "Little Le was about to participate in a ping-pong match.",
      "Because her opponent was very skilled, she was nervous before the match.",
      "",
      "Paul said to Little Le: “You can take off your shoes for the match.”",
      "Little Le asked him why.",
      "Paul said: “I've heard that ‘a person who walks around barefoot is not afraid of people wearing shoes.’”",
      "“If you take off your shoes, you won’t be afraid of her.”",
      "Little Le laughed and said: “That saying doesn’t mean that you should take off your shoes.”",
      "“But thanks, I’m not nervous at all now!”",
      "",
      "In fact, \"a person who walks around barefoot is not afraid of people wearing shoes\" means:",
